Parents: #605 #681 #689
Related: #632–#636 #637–#641 #647–#657 #658–#667 #691

## Problem
The roadmap now preserves source artifacts, schemas, strategy identities, feature coverage and many-thousands-column projection, but there is no single contract requiring every derived feature value to expose the exact chain of upstream artifact identities and transform identities that produced it.

This is distinct from row origin. `origin=synthetic` is insufficient if a consumer cannot determine which reconstruction member, bar transform, triangle synchronization policy, macro vintage, strategy compiler identity, population scenario, broker-style transform and imputation policy contributed to a particular feature.

## Canonical lineage DAG
Represent a feature product as a directed acyclic provenance graph `G=(V,E)`. Each node has at minimum:
- immutable node kind;
- canonical artifact/schema identity;
- software/transform identity and semantic version;
- normalized parameters/policy digest;
- point-in-time cutoff/availability rule;
- parent-node identities;
- environment identity where numerical behavior depends on it;
- output feature/group identity.

Define a canonical node digest recursively:

`h(v) = SHA256(canonical(kind_v, schema_v, transform_v, params_v, cutoff_v, sorted(parent_hashes_v)))`.

A final feature/group root is therefore content- and transformation-sensitive. Changing only the transform version or one parent identity changes the downstream root.

Planning sanity check run independently in the container: the same 5m-bar parent with `returns.v1` versus `returns.v2` produced different SHA-256 feature roots, confirming transform identity participates in the DAG identity.

## Required lineage coverage
At minimum support chains for:
1. raw/observed market evidence -> reconstructed member -> merged event tape;
2. event tape -> 1m/5m/15m/30m/1h/4h/1d bars -> indicators;
3. synchronized pair legs -> triangle/cross-currency features;
4. official release artifacts -> vintage-normalized calendar/forecast/positioning features;
5. feature snapshot -> v33 catalog record -> compiler/operator identity -> `strategy.FXES-*. *` response columns;
6. strategy/account ledgers -> `synthetic_flow.*` and population fingerprints;
7. verified real broker capture -> broker fingerprint -> optional bounded counterfactual broker-style transform;
8. nullable evidence feature -> dense-model imputation transform/mask;
9. all admitted groups -> final projected training view/label definition.

## Causal lineage
Lineage must retain availability/cutoff semantics, not only dependency names. For any final feature value at time `t`, every causal ancestor used as an input must satisfy its declared `available_at <= t` contract. Ex-post labels/revised vintages/broker future data may appear only in explicitly ex-post or target descendants.

## Atomic versus group lineage
A 10k+-column corpus cannot repeat a large JSON DAG in every cell. Support:
- feature-group lineage roots for shared transformations;
- compact per-column references to group root + field semantic identity;
- row/evidence-unit/member/scenario identity separately;
- optional expanded ancestry query for auditing a single feature/row.

The system must still answer: `why does this exact value exist?` without loading every upstream table.

## Semantic-change rules
A lineage identity must change when any scientifically meaningful dependency changes, including:
- source artifact/vintage/member/scenario;
- bar timeframe or partial/closed policy;
- triangle synchronization bound;
- transform/operator/compiler version;
- v33 catalog record identity;
- reason-code ontology;
- jurisdiction/execution/risk policy;
- population weights/scenario;
- broker fingerprint/transfer strength;
- imputation policy;
- label horizon/definition.

Pure physical relocation or compression may retain semantic lineage when #632–#636 establishes semantic equivalence.

## Graph invariants
Certification requires:
- acyclic graph;
- every non-root node's referenced parents exist;
- no orphan parent hashes;
- deterministic parent ordering in canonical serialization;
- same semantic DAG => same root under qualified environment/schema policy;
- one changed semantic ancestor => changed descendant root;
- no final feature namespace in #681 lacks a lineage root;
- no feature group can point to a future/noncausal ancestor in causal training views.

## Query and audit surfaces
Provide deterministic APIs/CLI to:
- resolve final column -> lineage root;
- expand lineage root -> complete ancestor graph;
- list all final features depending on a given source artifact/model/catalog record;
- compare two dataset/view roots and report first differing semantic ancestors;
- prove that a regenerated corpus uses the same lineage identities as a certified predecessor;
- export a compact lineage manifest for #691/#525 certification matrices.

## Negative controls
Must detect deliberately injected:
- swapped reconstruction member;
- revi
